---
// Volunteer Opportunities Section
---

<section class="bg-light" id="volunteer">
  <div class="container px-5">
    <div class="row gx-5 align-items-center justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-10">
        <div class="text-center mb-5">
          <h2 class="display-4 lh-1 mb-4">Volunteer Opportunities</h2>
          <p class="lead fw-normal text-muted">Join us in making a difference this winter season</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Volunteer Opportunity 1: Overnight Support -->
        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg mb-4">
          <div class="card-body p-5">
            <div class="text-center mb-4">
              <i class="bi-moon-stars icon-feature text-gradient d-block mb-3" style="font-size: 3rem;"></i>
              <h3 class="font-alt mb-3">Overnight Shelter Support Needed</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-muted mb-3">
              The Joshua House Warming Shelter in Newport is seeking caring, reliable volunteers to help staff the shelter overnight this winter season. The shelter, located at 501 Pleasant Street, provides a safe, warm place to sleep for up to eight guests each night during the cold-weather months (November–April).
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted mb-3">
              <strong>Volunteers will:</strong>
            </p>
            <ul class="text-muted mb-3">
              <li>Be present at the shelter overnight to ensure a welcoming, safe environment</li>
              <li>Assist guests with basic needs and follow established shelter guidelines</li>
              <li>Work alongside other volunteers to open, close, and maintain the space</li>
            </ul>
            <!--
			<p class="text-muted mb-3">
              Shifts will generally run from evening through early morning, and volunteers will receive orientation and ongoing support.
            </p>
			-->
			<p class="text-muted mb-3">
              <b>Training for the role will be 2 consecutive nights</b> from 6:00-8:00 at the Warming Shelter on <b>November 19 & 20</b>.  Food will be provided. 
            </p>
			
            <p class="text-muted mb-4">
              This is a volunteer/unpaid role — but one that offers a chance to make a direct, meaningful difference in the lives of community members experiencing homelessness during Vermont's harsh winter.
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted">
              If you can commit to one or more nights per week (or even occasionally), please contact <a href="mailto:plfarrow58@gmail.com" class="text-gradient fw-bold">Pam Farrow</a> or <a href="mailto:rick.uffordchase@newportvermont.org" class="text-gradient fw-bold">Rick Ufford-Chase</a> to learn more or sign up.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Volunteer Opportunity 2: Leadership -->
        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg mb-4">
          <div class="card-body p-5">
            <div class="text-center mb-4">
              <i class="bi-person-check icon-feature text-gradient d-block mb-3" style="font-size: 3rem;"></i>
              <h3 class="font-alt mb-3">Help Lead the Joshua House Warming Shelter</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-muted mb-3">
              The Joshua House Warming Shelter in Newport is seeking dedicated volunteers to help organize and oversee operations for this year's 8-bed seasonal cold-weather shelter, located at 501 Pleasant Street. The shelter is expected to open in late November and operate through April.
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted mb-3">
              <strong>We're looking for one or more people who can take the lead on:</strong>
            </p>
            <ul class="text-muted mb-3">
              <li>Coordinating shelter operations and schedules</li>
              <li>Recruiting and preparing volunteers</li>
              <li>Ensuring smooth day-to-day functioning</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-muted mb-4">
              This role is ideal for someone who is well-organized, a strong communicator, and ready to make a meaningful impact in the community.
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted">
              If you're passionate about helping others and can dedicate time over the winter season, please reach out to <a href="mailto:jhinctim@gmail.com" class="text-gradient fw-bold">Tim Daley</a> or <a href="mailto:rick.uffordchase@newportvermont.org" class="text-gradient fw-bold">Rick Ufford-Chase</a> to learn more or get involved.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Volunteer Opportunity 3: Work Days -->
        <div class="card border-0 shadow-lg mb-4">
          <div class="card-body p-5">
            <div class="text-center mb-4">
              <i class="bi-tools icon-feature text-gradient d-block mb-3" style="font-size: 3rem;"></i>
              <h3 class="font-alt mb-3">Volunteer Work Days</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-muted mb-3">
              Join us on <strong>Saturdays at 9:00 AM</strong> at 501 Pleasant Street, Newport to help prepare the Joshua House Warming Shelter for the upcoming winter season!
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted mb-3">
              We're looking for volunteers to assist with hands-on projects such as cleaning, organizing, light repairs, setup, and other tasks to get the 8-bed seasonal shelter ready to open in late November.
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted mb-4">
              No special skills required — just bring a willingness to help and a can-do attitude! Whether you can come once or join us regularly, your time and effort will make a real difference for community members in need this winter.
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted">
              For more information or to sign up, please contact <a href="mailto:rick.uffordchase@newportvermont.org" class="text-gradient fw-bold">Rick Ufford-Chase</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>